## Authentication

Accounts, JWT sign-in and the email / mobile flows live in `app/auth/` (routes under `/auth`).
Set the secrets from `.env.example` in `.env` before starting: `AUTH_JWT_SECRET` is required and
`docker compose up` refuses to start without it. Secrets are read from the environment only.

| Route | What it does |
|---|---|
| `POST /auth/register` | Create an account (email, password, optional `phone` in E.164{% if auth.registration.custom_fields %}, plus your custom fields{% endif %}) |
| `POST /auth/login` | Email + password -> access and refresh token |
| `POST /auth/refresh` | Rotate the refresh token (a reused token revokes its whole chain) |
| `POST /auth/logout` | Revoke a refresh token chain |
| `GET /auth/me` | The signed-in account |
| `DELETE /auth/me` | {{ "Delete the account and its data" if auth.deletion_mode == "hard" else "Disable the account (soft delete)" }} |
| `POST /auth/change-password` | Change password and sign out everywhere |
| `POST /auth/email/verify`, `POST /auth/email/resend-verification` | Confirm an email address{{ " (required before sign-in)" if auth.registration.email_verification_required }} |
{% if auth.password_reset.email_magic_link %}
| `POST /auth/magic-link/request`, `POST /auth/magic-link/consume` | Passwordless sign-in by emailed link |
{% endif %}
{% if auth.password_reset.sms_otp %}
| `POST /auth/phone/verify/request`, `POST /auth/phone/verify/confirm` | Verify a phone number by SMS code |
| `POST /auth/otp/request`, `POST /auth/otp/verify` | Sign in with an SMS code (verified numbers only) |
{% endif %}
{% if invitations %}
| `POST/GET /auth/invitations`, `DELETE /auth/invitations/{id}` | Admins email one-time registration links{{ " (registration is invite-only)" if auth.registration.invite_only }} |
{% endif %}
{% if auth.password_reset.email_magic_link or auth.password_reset.sms_otp %}
| `POST /auth/password-reset/request`, `POST /auth/password-reset/confirm` | Reset a password by {{ "emailed link" if auth.password_reset.email_magic_link }}{{ " or " if auth.password_reset.email_magic_link and auth.password_reset.sms_otp }}{{ "SMS code" if auth.password_reset.sms_otp }} |
{% endif %}

Send `Authorization: Bearer <access_token>` to authenticated routes. Protect your own routes with
`CurrentUser` and `require_roles("...")` from `app/auth/deps.py`.
{% if auth.app_url %}

Emailed links point at `{{ auth.app_url }}` (`/verify-email`, `/magic-link`, `/reset-password`, each with `?token=`);
your frontend should read the token and call the matching API route.
{% endif %}

Limits: sign-in {{ auth.login_rate_limit }}, registration {{ auth.register_rate_limit }}, email / SMS requests {{ auth.reset_rate_limit }} per client address.
They are counted in process memory, so they are per worker.

